# Versioning

Semver in `VERSION` (one line, `X.Y.Z`). The release workflow refuses a tag
that does not match it. Bump it with every shipped change, once per chat
session.

Keep three places in sync:

- `VERSION`
- `README.md` badge on line 3: `![Version](https://img.shields.io/badge/version-X.Y.Z-4EAA25)`
- `CHANGELOG.md`: a new section at the top

| Bump | When |
| --- | --- |
| patch | fix, refactor, docs, CI |
| minor | a new command, option or config key with a default |
| major | a breaking change: a command or argument removed or renamed, a config key changed, a linked site laid out differently (see AGENTS.md rule 1) |

Changelog format: `### vX.Y.Z (YYYY-MM-DD)`, `*` bullets, a bolded area
ending with a colon, present tense, what the user notices. Areas: `wpcore:`,
`Installer:`, `Fix:`, `Docs:`, `Repo:`. No em dashes. The release notes are
the tag's section, and webtimeless.cloud's changelog reads the same file.
